<file path="MICROSERVICE_RULES.md">
# Microservice Architecture Rules

## 1. Edge And Gateway

- The public HTTP edge is the Express/Node.js API Gateway in `api-gateway`.
- Frontend and mobile clients call backend APIs through the gateway.
- Services should communicate on the Docker internal network unless a port is explicitly exposed for local debugging.
- Gateway routes requests only; it must not own business state.

## 2. Gateway Does Not Call Infrastructure Directly

- Wrong: Gateway -> PostgreSQL / Redis / Milvus / MinIO.
- Correct: Gateway -> Service -> Infrastructure.
- Gateway talks to services over HTTP.

## 3. Service-To-Service Communication

- Sync communication uses REST over the internal Docker network.
- Internal service calls use `x-internal-api-key`.
- Async work currently uses Redis and Celery.
- Services should not call each other through the public API Gateway.

## 4. Data Ownership

- `user-service` owns `users`, auth data, staff/admin/patron identity, and profile fields.
- `access-service` owns `access_logs`, patron inside/outside state, access stats, SSE, and WebSocket realtime.
- `face-recognition-service` owns face enrollment, embeddings, Milvus, MinIO evidence, and recognition jobs.
- `borrow-service` owns borrow/book data and asks `user-service` or `access-service` when it needs user/access state.
- `schedule-service` owns library zones, shifts, schedule assignments, attendance, and schedule audit logs.
- A service that needs data owned by another service should call that service's internal API instead of querying its tables directly.

## 5. Face And Access Boundary

- Face login only authenticates and returns tokens.
- Camera entry/exit and kiosk flows are responsible for recording physical access.
- Entry camera writes `entry` events only.
- Exit camera writes `exit` events only.
- Kiosk may auto-toggle entry/exit based on current user status.
- Face worker sends recognition/access results to `access-service` through `POST /internal/access/recognition-events`.
- `access-service` is the source of truth for access logs and patron inside/outside state.
- Legacy access routes in `face-recognition-service` are deprecated while gateway `/api/access/*` routes to `access-service`.

## 6. Internal API Key Pattern

- Service-to-service calls use header `x-internal-api-key`.
- Do not use end-user JWTs for internal service authority.
- The key is configured through environment variables and must match across services.

## 7. Shared State And Redis

- Redis is used for Celery broker/result backend, temporary camera frame cache, throttling/cooldowns, and pub/sub events.
- Each service owns its Redis keys and should use clear prefixes.
- Gateway rate limiting should remain at gateway/edge level and not require DB access.

## 8. Configuration

- Configuration must come from environment variables.
- Keep `.env.example` files complete enough for clone-and-run.
- Do not commit `.env`, `.env.local`, test output, build artifacts, or local cache folders.
- Docker Compose is the local integration source of truth.

## 9. Health And Readiness

- Each service should expose an alive endpoint.
- Services with dependencies should expose readiness checks when possible.
- Smoke checks after changes should include gateway `/healthz`, `/openapi.json`, auth login, face login, access stats, and borrow books.
- Run `node scripts/check-service-boundaries.js` before pushing service-boundary changes.

## 10. Validation And Shutdown

- Each service validates its own inputs.
- Services should handle shutdown signals and close DB/Redis/Milvus/MinIO clients cleanly.
</file>

<file path="scripts/check-service-boundaries.js">
const fs = require('fs');
const path = require('path');

const root = path.resolve(__dirname, '..');

const rules = [
  {
    service: 'user-service',
    include: ['src'],
    extensions: ['.ts'],
    forbidden: [
      { pattern: /\bpatron_faces\b/i, reason: 'user-service must publish user events instead of deleting face tables' },
      { pattern: /\baccess_logs\b/i, reason: 'user-service must not read or delete access logs' },
      { pattern: /\bborrow_records\b/i, reason: 'user-service must not read borrow records' },
    ],
    allow: [
      /config\.ts$/,
    ],
  },
  {
    service: 'borrow-service',
    include: ['src'],
    extensions: ['.ts'],
    forbidden: [
      { pattern: /\busers\b/i, reason: 'borrow-service must call user-service instead of using users table' },
      { pattern: /\baccess_logs\b/i, reason: 'borrow-service must call access-service instead of using access logs' },
      { pattern: /\bpatron_access_states\b/i, reason: 'borrow-service must call access-service instead of using access state tables' },
    ],
    allow: [
      /UserServiceClient\.ts$/,
      /AccessServiceClient\.ts$/,
      /routes[\\/]borrow\.routes\.ts$/,
      /config\.ts$/,
    ],
  },
  {
    service: 'access-service',
    include: ['src'],
    extensions: ['.ts'],
    forbidden: [
      { pattern: /\bborrow_records\b/i, reason: 'access-service must not read borrow records' },
      { pattern: /\bbook_copies\b/i, reason: 'access-service must not read book copies' },
      { pattern: /\bbooks\b/i, reason: 'access-service must not read books' },
      { pattern: /@Entity\([^)]*users/i, reason: 'access-service must not map the users table' },
    ],
    allow: [
      /UserServiceClient\.ts$/,
    ],
  },
  {
    service: 'schedule-service',
    include: ['src'],
    extensions: ['.ts'],
    forbidden: [
      { pattern: /\bborrow_records\b/i, reason: 'schedule-service must not read borrow records' },
      { pattern: /\baccess_logs\b/i, reason: 'schedule-service must not read access logs' },
      { pattern: /\bpatron_access_states\b/i, reason: 'schedule-service must not read access state tables' },
      { pattern: /@Entity\([^)]*users/i, reason: 'schedule-service must not map the users table' },
    ],
    allow: [
      /UserServiceClient\.ts$/,
      /ScheduleService\.ts$/,
      /config\.ts$/,
    ],
  },
  {
    service: 'face-recognition-service',
    include: ['api', 'infra', 'worker'],
    extensions: ['.py'],
    forbidden: [
      { pattern: /class\s+UserModel\b/, reason: 'face-recognition-service must not map the users table' },
      { pattern: /class\s+AccessLogModel\b/, reason: 'face-recognition-service must not map access logs' },
      { pattern: /__tablename__\s*=\s*["']users["']/, reason: 'face-recognition-service must not own users' },
      { pattern: /__tablename__\s*=\s*["']access_logs["']/, reason: 'face-recognition-service must not own access logs' },
      { pattern: /select\(UserModel|update\(UserModel/, reason: 'face-recognition-service must call user-service instead of querying users' },
      { pattern: /select\(AccessLogModel|INSERT\s+INTO\s+access_logs/i, reason: 'face-recognition-service must call access-service instead of querying access logs' },
    ],
    allow: [
      /api[\\/]routers[\\/]access\.py$/,
    ],
  },
  {
    service: 'ai-service',
    include: ['src'],
    extensions: ['.ts'],
    forbidden: [
      { pattern: /\busers\b/i, reason: 'ai-service must call user-service instead of querying users' },
      { pattern: /\baccess_logs\b/i, reason: 'ai-service must call access-service instead of querying access logs' },
      { pattern: /\bborrow_records\b/i, reason: 'ai-service must call borrow-service instead of querying borrow records' },
      { pattern: /\bbook_copies\b/i, reason: 'ai-service must call borrow-service instead of querying inventory tables' },
      { pattern: /\bstaff_schedules\b/i, reason: 'ai-service must call schedule-service instead of querying schedules' },
    ],
    allow: [
      /config\.ts$/,
      /entities[\\/]Ai/,
      /migrations[\\/]/,
    ],
  },
];

function walk(dir, files = []) {
  for (const entry of fs.readdirSync(dir, { withFileTypes: true })) {
    if (['node_modules', 'dist', '__pycache__', '.pytest_cache'].includes(entry.name)) continue;
    const fullPath = path.join(dir, entry.name);
    if (entry.isDirectory()) {
      walk(fullPath, files);
    } else {
      files.push(fullPath);
    }
  }
  return files;
}

const violations = [];

for (const rule of rules) {
  const serviceRoot = path.join(root, rule.service);
  for (const includePath of rule.include) {
    const scanRoot = path.join(serviceRoot, includePath);
    if (!fs.existsSync(scanRoot)) continue;
    for (const file of walk(scanRoot)) {
      if (!rule.extensions.includes(path.extname(file))) continue;
      const relative = path.relative(serviceRoot, file);
      if (rule.allow.some((allowed) => allowed.test(relative))) continue;
      const content = fs.readFileSync(file, 'utf8');
      for (const forbidden of rule.forbidden) {
        if (forbidden.pattern.test(content)) {
          violations.push({
            service: rule.service,
            file: path.relative(root, file),
            reason: forbidden.reason,
          });
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

if (violations.length) {
  console.error('Service boundary violations found:');
  for (const violation of violations) {
    console.error(`- ${violation.file}: ${violation.reason}`);
  }
  process.exit(1);
}

console.log('Service boundary check passed.');
</file>

